  Cell["The modern name reflects support for diagram pairs, factorization \
rows and completed external-mass pairs. New notebooks should use \
PrepareAmplitudes.", "Notes"], Cell["The compatibility call has the same \
default compact output and optional detailed reports. It does not restore an \
earlier neural simplifier or apply a different set of assumptions.",
   "Notes"], Cell["Options", "NotesSection"],
  Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell["Option", "TableHeader"],
       Cell["Default", "TableHeader"], Cell["Meaning", "TableHeader"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"PolePreference\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Reference and \
representation preference shared by preparation and completion. Automatic \
compares or inherits admissible choices; \"AllPhysical\", \"AllSpurious\" and \
\"Mixed\" bias pole forms, while cyclic/common/independent reference choices \
and None are also available. Required checks remain unchanged.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ExternalParticles\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Ordered external particle \
names when compact amplitude pairs no longer retain the process. Automatic \
uses recorded metadata or only unambiguous model matches; equal masses alone \
never establish identical species.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"FermionHelicities\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", "}"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Leg-to-helicity rules or an association \
specifying massless Dirac external states for Feynman conversion. Required \
missing massless-fermion helicities are reported rather than guessed.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MaxReferenceChoices\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Maximum reference \
assignments tried during bounded preparation. Automatic currently allows up \
to 64 trials, subject to the shared reference and item clocks; this is not \
exhaustive global minimization.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ReferenceTimeConstraint\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Budget for reference \
comparisons in checking, or reference-choice search in preparation. Automatic \
bounds this work; preparation shares it with the remaining per-item clock \
rather than adding an unlimited extra search.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"InternalOnShell\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"True"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether preparation may use declared constructive \
internal-channel masses in each item's numerator. True never puts PropDen \
denominators on shell and never transfers one diagram's assumptions to \
another; False leaves internal-shell reductions disabled.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MaxSteps\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Maximum improving \
identity-search steps during preparation. Automatic scales the bounded effort \
to the workload; 0 retains deterministic contraction, spinor and permitted \
scalar-shell reductions while skipping the search.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MaxCandidates\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Bound on candidate \
identity edits considered during preparation. Automatic selects a finite \
workload-dependent allowance rather than searching every possible route.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"TimeConstraint\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Maximum elapsed time \
allowed by the operation or stage. Where Automatic is supported it selects a \
finite workload-dependent budget; explicit seconds or supported Infinity \
override it. A timeout is reported, never treated as a successful amplitude."\
, "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MomentumConservation\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"True"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether identities may use the complete declared \
external momentum sum. The operation uses the known external-leg list rather \
than imposing unrelated internal cut conditions.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Parallelization\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Whether independent items \
or checks may use local Wolfram workers. Automatic uses suitable parallel \
work within available resources; False requests serial evaluation, and result \
order is retained.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MaxKernels\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Maximum local Wolfram \
worker kernels available to parallel stages. Automatic respects processor \
availability and license limits; 1 requests serial execution. Worker setup \
and expression transfer can outweigh small jobs.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ProgressReporting\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"True"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether preparation and construction stages \
display their progress. False suppresses the live stage display without \
changing the algebra or validation.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ProgressFunction\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Optional callback \
receiving stage progress information. Automatic uses the normal progress \
display; callbacks are evaluated on the main kernel rather than independently \
